        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-12T10:01:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for catching this. Since this algorithm serves only as the subject algorithm in multi-alg dice and both the authority/subject algorithm in non-multi-alg DICE, inlining it might make future modifications difficult if we decide to switch to a different algorithm.\n\nWhat about `VM_KEY_ALGORITHM` (adjusted in the lates PS)? As the primary goal of the algorithm is to transition from various algorithms in vendor\u0027s DICE chain to this specific algorithm used within different components of a VM.",
      "parentUuid": "2ba91425_0beb2f0f",
      "revId": "8f0de0734f023d57de93307f17b36b102b57d236",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad85d077_78ed575d",
        "filename": "libs/dice/open_dice/src/dice.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-12T19:56:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That makes sense but then it doesn\u0027t seem to git in the open_dice library since it\u0027s VM-specific. It\u0027s getting to the point that the VM libraries below might just want to reference Ed25519 directly?",
      "parentUuid": "9bbfecbd_95d12a36",
      "revId": "8f0de0734f023d57de93307f17b36b102b57d236",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f6d020b9_37345059",
        "filename": "libs/dice/open_dice/src/dice.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 88,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-12T20:54:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e It\u0027s getting to the point that the VM libraries below might just want to reference Ed25519 directly?\n\nWhile it\u0027s possible, directly referencing Ed25519 might limit flexibility in the future. The parameter is currently used by both clients of open-dice (as in this cl) and open-dice itself (aosp/3342291). If we remove the parameter and inline the algorithm in all call sites, although it work for now, it would complicate matters if we want to switch to a different algorithm later.\n\nI think this dice wrapper is already VM-specific since it\u0027s in the AVF repo and only visible to VM libraries. However, I\u0027m also open to rename it to something less VM-specific, do you have any suggestion?",
      "parentUuid": "ad85d077_78ed575d",
      "revId": "8f0de0734f023d57de93307f17b36b102b57d236",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
